If a clinician starts a methadone-treatment for a patient and an initial-follow-up-period has a duration and the duration includes 1 week then the clinician should consider a follow-up after 2 days during the initial-follow-up-period.
If a clinician starts a methadone-treatment for a patient and an initial-follow-up-period has a duration and the duration includes 1 week then the clinician should consider a follow-up after 3 days during the initial-follow-up-period.
If a clinician increases a methadone-dosage for a patient and an initial-follow-up-period has a duration and the duration includes 1 week then the clinician should consider a follow-up after 2 days during the initial-follow-up-period.
If a clinician increases a methadone-dosage for a patient and an initial-follow-up-period has a duration and the duration includes 1 week then the clinician should consider a follow-up after 3 days during the initial-follow-up-period.
